  {
   "id": "CSrqMDz6AQAJ",
   "from": "Dan Ridley-Ellis",
   "author": "93c37e914cc10dab",
   "date": "2017-11-23T23:46:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: Small error in spec function (and proposed fix)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>I confirmed there is a problem. The attached example is the result of 2000 mathematically generated damped sine waves. Analysis is over a 2 second period at 44.1 kHz sampling rate - which means an odd number of points. Frequency accuracy error is biased by half an fft bin at the top end - and this is the result of an error in how the x vector is calculated within spec.</div><div><br></div><div>Script along these lines works</div><div><div>        </div><div>        x = seq(0, (f/2), length.out = length(y) + 1)/1000 </div><div>        x = head(x, n = length(x)-1)</div><div><br></div><div>where y is the vector of of FFT amplitudes, already cut in half from what comes out of fft()        </div><div>        </div></div><div>Dan</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, 21 November 2017 00:01:03 UTC, Dan Ridley-Ellis  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Hi</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n<span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I&#39;ve been throwing a bunch of mathematically\r\ngenerated waves at the spec function and I&#39;ve noticed that it makes a small\r\nerror when the wave has an odd number of points in the time domain. \r\n I think this caused by the way that the vector of frequency bins is\r\ncalculated in the spec function.  </span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">The error means that frequencies at the high end are, on average, in error by half the width of a fft frequency bin when there an odd number of points in the time domain.</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">If there an even number of points, no problems  </span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">In the spec function there is the code for the frequency bins x: </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> if\r\n(is.null(at)) {</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> \r\n        x &lt;- seq(0, (f/2) - (f/n), length.out =\r\nn%/%2)/1000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> \r\n      }</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> \r\n      else {</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> \r\n        x &lt;- seq(0, (f/2) - (f/wl), length.out =\r\nn%/%2)/1000</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> \r\n      }</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">This seems to work better (but I am not sure why)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">  if (is.null(at)) {</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">          x &lt;- seq(0, (f/2) - (f/n) - n%%2, length.out = n%/%2)/1000</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">        }</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">        else {</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">          x &lt;- seq(0, (f/2) - (f/wl) </span></font><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px\">- n%%2</span><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">, length.out = n%/%2)/1000</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">        }</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">Dan</span></font></p></div></blockquote></div>"
